Part - 01

Day 6 Notes – Next.js + Tailwind

1.React vs Next.js
React → Library for building user interfaces
Next.js → Framework built on top of React that adds routing, structure, and performance features

2.What Next.js Gives You
-File-based routing (pages based on folder structure)
-Better performance options (SSR, SSG)
-Easier production setup
-Popular for complete web applications

3.Tailwind CSS
-A utility-first CSS framework.
-Instead of writing custom CSS, you use ready-made small classes directly in your code.

4.Examples of utility classes:
text-center
p-4
bg-blue-500
flex


5.Why Developers Use Them
Next.js → Structure + performance + easier full applications
Tailwind → Faster styling + consistent design + less custom CSS

6.Security Note:
Never put sensitive keys in variables that start with NEXT_PUBLIC_
(Those become visible in the browser)

Key Point:
Next.js = React with extra powers

Tailwind = Fast styling using utility classes

